### PDF

- **{pdf.download_link} –**Admin can give permission to download PDFs to the users and share encrypted URLs that the user can access.

### Quiz

- **{quiz_result}** – It shows the results of the Quiz.

Would you like a simple horizontal Email **Opt-in Form**using **Fluent Forms**on your WordPress site? Just read along with this simple guide to learn how to apply this feature.

- The next step is to navigate to **Fluent Forms →** **Tools →** **Import Forms**.

![](https://wpmanageninja.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/05/Tools-‹-Fluent-Forms-Test-—-WordPress.png)

- Then click on this [link](https://share.getcloudapp.com/rRunQgWj) to import this form. You have to edit the form and connect the form with the provider of your mailing list. And copy the **Shortcode.**

![](https://wpmanageninja.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/05/Editor-Fluentform-17.png)

- Use the Page Editor to edit your Template/Page where you want to display the form. Then you need to add a **Section.**

```
.section{
     background-color:#f0f0f0;
     align-items:center;
 }
```

- Now it’s time to add a **Heading.**You may want to change the tag to H2(or H3 etc).

```
.heading{
     color:#566d8f;
     font-size:20px;
}
```

- Then you have to add a shortcode component. And paste this shortcode taken from the earlier step.

```
.shortcode{
     margin-top:20px;
     width:100%;
     max-width:600px;
}
```

That’s all! This is how you can customize a simple horizontal email opt-in form.

